# The `build` target does `COPY . .`, so anything here lands in an image layer. Without this
# file that included `.env` - internal mirror hostnames and, per .env.example, a slot for a
# GitHub token - which anyone who shares or exports the image then publishes. That is the exact
# disclosure class AGENTS.md forbids, and it survives deleting the file afterwards.
#
# It also cuts the build context from gigabytes (.pixi holds a whole materialised environment)
# to something that transfers.

# Secrets and local configuration. `.env.example` is the committed template and is fine.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
devenv.local.nix
.ponytail-active

# Version control and build output.
.git
.gitignore
target
result
result-*
dist
stage
docs/book

# Tool state, none of which belongs in an image.
.direnv
.devenv
.pixi
node_modules
__pycache__
